Refs ed3c/soodles#53

This atom removes the recovery deadlock observed after Issue #51 without replaying its provider writes.

Behavioral change:

- `landing resume` may migrate a completed checkpoint from `awaiting_reconcile` as well as `reconciling`;
- every claim field except the selected verifier digest remains fixed;
- a cloud-only delivery with no candidate path, branch, or worktree registration persists `cleanup_intent.mode=no_op` and `phase=reconciling` before Git synchronization;
- any branch or registration refuses the no-op path;
- existing Noodle-owned cleanup remains unchanged for resources that exist;
- terminal receipts expose `local.cleanup_mode`.

Focused evidence before PR:

- 108 discovered unit tests passed with no skips;
- cleanup recovery oracle passed five existing SIGKILL/recovery cases plus one new `cloud_noop` case;
- the new case migrated from `awaiting_reconcile`, emitted zero provider requests, invoked no worktree deletion, and left zero residue;
- the updated `verify-soodles` skill passed its structural validator.

The historical #51 RED receipt remains unchanged. This candidate does not claim authority for its own landing or for the eventual #51 terminal reconciliation.

## Landing observation

- PR #54 merged exactly once as `008d5e98e092f3c13a04a501188dc41cb73094c7`; Issue #53 closed as completed.
- The independently selected merged verifier accepted migration from `awaiting_reconcile` with zero provider requests.
- Reconcile mechanically proved the candidate path, branch, and worktree registration were all absent, then durably persisted `cleanup_intent.mode=no_op` and `phase=reconciling`.
- The subsequent Git fetch was refused with exit 128 in this environment. Therefore this receipt is `RECONCILING_BLOCKED_GIT_FETCH`, not `RESOLVED`.
- Merge and close were not replayed. No synthetic worktree was created.

[Delivery receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/4fd08bcfa4f0e6a029e9903dca996ede31bdee99/docs/experiments/cloud-noop-53/delivery/delivery-receipt.json), [checkpoint](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/4fd08bcfa4f0e6a029e9903dca996ede31bdee99/docs/experiments/cloud-noop-53/delivery/checkpoint.json), and [reconcile result](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/4fd08bcfa4f0e6a029e9903dca996ede31bdee99/docs/experiments/cloud-noop-53/delivery/reconcile-result.json) preserve the boundary.

Safe continuation: after Git transport is materially restored, invoke `landing reconcile` once with this exact checkpoint, verifier, and Noodle binary.

issue.body:
## Intent

Remove the single recovery deadlock observed after Issue #51 provider delivery. A cloud Session may legitimately have no local candidate branch, worktree path or registration. The landing owner must migrate the completed checkpoint to an independently accepted verifier and record that proven absence as no-op cleanup without replaying provider writes.

This atom owns the two inseparable transitions in the same durable owner:

1. verifier migration from `awaiting_reconcile` after completed provider writes;
2. reconciliation when the candidate path, branch and registration were never created locally.

It does not rerun the Issue #51 behavior comparison, add a scheduler, create a synthetic worktree, change provider identity or replay merge/close.

## Observed defect

The preserved [Issue #51 delivery receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/9b7a33976a9cf35b0d1cc807d03d4659d6f0fbac/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/delivery-receipt.json) records:

- provider merge and Issue closure complete;
- checkpoint phase `awaiting_reconcile`;
- `writes_offered == ["merge", "close"]`;
- candidate branch/worktree absent;
- old owner refusal `worktree.path=missing before cleanup intent`;
- Git fetch not reached.

The current `landing resume` accepts only `reconciling`. The old verifier cannot reach that phase, while a corrected verifier cannot replace the pinned digest. This is a closed recovery deadlock.

## Executable contract

### Positive

A supervisor-selected corrected verifier may migrate a checkpoint from `awaiting_reconcile` only when:

- `merge_sha` and `issue_closed_at` are present;
- `writes_offered` is exactly `["merge", "close"]`;
- every claim field except `verifier_sha256` is byte-for-byte unchanged;
- the verifier digest changes to the selected implementation;
- the result emits no provider request.

During reconcile, when the expected candidate path and branch are absent, Git worktree registration must also prove absent. The owner durably records a no-op cleanup observation and `phase=reconciling` before Git synchronization. After exact merge ancestry, fast-forward, clean root and repeated absence checks, it may emit `classification=RESOLVED`, `phase=resolved`, `next=null`.

### Planted negatives

The owner must refuse without cleanup/provider effects when:

- provider completion evidence or offered-write history is incomplete;
- verifier digest is unchanged;
- any non-verifier claim identity changes;
- candidate path is absent but its branch still exists before cleanup intent;
- the candidate branch is registered at any path;
- a branch/worktree identity is foreign or moved;
- final path, branch or registration is present.

Existing interrupted-cleanup, lock, legacy-checkpoint and Noodle-owned worktree controls remain green.

## Evidence and landing

- Preserve the old #51 refusal as defect RED; do not rewrite its receipt.
- Add focused unit and recovery-oracle controls for the corrected boundary.
- Run canonical acceptance once on the exact final candidate through existing `runtime.yml`.
- Deliver this Issue through the preselected external landing owner, not candidate code.
- After the fix is independently landed, select its immutable merged verifier for the existing #51 checkpoint.
- Never replay #51 merge or close. If the original carrier or Git transport is unavailable, retain that exact blocker instead of claiming `RESOLVED`.

## Completion

This Issue is complete only when its own candidate is merged/closed with normal reconciliation. Resolution of the historical #51 checkpoint is a post-landing recovery observation: either a real terminal receipt or a preserved carrier/transport blocker.

## Landing observation

- PR #54 merged exactly once as `008d5e98e092f3c13a04a501188dc41cb73094c7`; Issue #53 closed as completed.
- The independently selected merged verifier accepted migration from `awaiting_reconcile` with zero provider requests.
- Reconcile mechanically proved the candidate path, branch, and worktree registration were all absent, then durably persisted `cleanup_intent.mode=no_op` and `phase=reconciling`.
- The subsequent Git fetch was refused with exit 128 in this environment. Therefore this receipt is `RECONCILING_BLOCKED_GIT_FETCH`, not `RESOLVED`.
- Merge and close were not replayed. No synthetic worktree was created.

[Delivery receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/4fd08bcfa4f0e6a029e9903dca996ede31bdee99/docs/experiments/cloud-noop-53/delivery/delivery-receipt.json), [checkpoint](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/4fd08bcfa4f0e6a029e9903dca996ede31bdee99/docs/experiments/cloud-noop-53/delivery/checkpoint.json), and [reconcile result](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/4fd08bcfa4f0e6a029e9903dca996ede31bdee99/docs/experiments/cloud-noop-53/delivery/reconcile-result.json) preserve the boundary.

